f
tr_fus_dt_hot.gs
c
! DT-fusion regression case at 10 keV (model_pnf=1) for kyoshimi TR.
! Physically equivalent to the bpsi trx reference capture in
! test_run/baselines/tr_fus_dt_hot/ (see SOURCE.md).  Analytic geometry
! (modelg=2, self-contained, no eq dependency); species e/D/T/He4.
!
! NOT byte-identical to the reference deck, and must not be made so: PROFN2
! is a bare scalar here and PROFN2(NSM) in trx, so the single value below
! covers every species while the reference deck has to spell all four out.
! Writing four values here still "works" -- gfortran assigns as it parses,
! so the first lands and the rest raise a cosmetic `## PARM INPUT ERROR.`
! -- which makes the mistake invisible.  Leave it as one value.
!
! This is the PRIMARY Task 7 oracle, in place of the 1 keV tr_fus_dt case.
! The 1 keV case was chosen when a 10 keV variant appeared to run away
! thermally -- but that runaway was an artefact of a 1e6 unit error in the
! reference's reaction rate (svnf_* tables are cm^3/s, consumed as m^3/s).
! With that corrected the hot case is stable and carries ~1.8e5x more fusion
! signal (rel. WPT 1.11e-3 against 6.2e-9).  It is somewhat WORSE conditioned
! (1e-12 perturbation amplified 2.32 against 1.00), which does not matter at
! this distance from the tolerance -- it still leaves ~4.3e5x of margin.
!
! The numbers above are reference-side and are derived in
! test_run/baselines/tr_fus_dt_hot/SOURCE.md; that file is authoritative if
! these ever disagree.  NTMAX=5 is kept from the cold case.
   modelg=2
   RR=8.481D0
   RA=2.574D0
   RKAP=1.816D0
   RDLT=0.3478D0
   BB=5.953D0
   NSMAX=4
   PN=0.1D0,0.045D0,0.045D0,0.005D0
   PNS=0.01D0,0.0045D0,0.0045D0,0.0005D0
   PT=10.0D0,10.0D0,10.0D0,10.0D0
   PTS=1.0D0,1.0D0,1.0D0,1.0D0
   PROFN2=0.15D0
   model_pnf=1
   DT=0.02D0
   NRMAX=50
   NTMAX=5
   NTSTEP=5
   RIPS=2.D0
   RIPE=3.D0
r
q
